\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{From degrees to Berry flux}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{A general Hermitian symbol has no canonical vector-valued degree model. At the sampled
vertices, its negative spectral subspaces form a finite family of subspaces of one complex
Hilbert space. Choose orthonormal bases for two neighboring subspaces of equal dimension.
If their overlap matrix has nonzero determinant, its phase is defined for those bases. What integer do these
phases give on a closed triangle surface of a grid of any dimension #{n\ge 2}?
When #{n\ge 3}, how do the boundaries of three-dimensional simplices meeting singular
vertices cancel against the other simplex boundaries in a closed three-chain?}
